    "body": "If you upload the data file to a public location, I can take a look.\r\n\r\nAbsent the data, I can offer the following observations:\r\nThe LRS / t-Tuple test runtimes can be particularly variable. Is the longest repeated substring very large for this data sample? If so, then this could be an instance of it taking a very long time, rather than it hanging. (I've seen all sorts of failure modes for this tool, but I've never witnessed an infinite loop, but it is certainly possible that something strange is going on here...)",
